  - target: term/industrial-accident-question
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The chapter explicitly directs the accident question to chapter 66 while retaining the special
      accident-is-injury case.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol11-ch69/0006
      quote: "69022 If the accident question arises for the first time on an IIDB claim, the DM should consider
        the\nquestion as in DMG Chapter 66. If the case is of the 'accident is the injury' type the DM must be satisfied\n\
        that the claimant suffered personal injury by accident before a favourable accident decision can be\n\n\
        given1.\n\n\n                                                                                          \
        \        1 R(I) 7/73"
      locator: DMG 69022
  - target: term/dmg-decision-maker
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source assigns the outcome decision and its underlying questions to the DM.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol11-ch69/0006
      quote: "69020 DMs will give an outcome decision on the claim which consists of a statement to the effect that\n\
        the claimant is either entitled or not entitled to benefit. In arriving at an outcome decision, the DM must\n\
        consider various questions. For IIDB, these questions fall into two categories\n\n\n1. non medical questions
        such as employed earners employment, rate of benefit 1and\n\n\n2. medical questions such as diagnosis, relevant
        loss of faculty and disablement assessment.\n\n\nNote: See DMG Chapter 01 for further guidance on IIDB decisions.\n\
        \n\n                                                                                       1 SS CB Act 92,
        s 94"
      locator: DMG 69020
